          "body": "[Local Codex: code-review] Do not repeatedly cancel slow Booklet enrichment\n\nReviewed head: 8698a1e640ca70fcbeb43f1eddbd04ca2aa0718b\n\nEach five-second snapshot replaces the entire Booklet-enrichment observable with switchMap. Booklet requests use ref-counted sharing, so if a Booklet takes longer than the snapshot interval, each new snapshot unsubscribes and aborts the preceding read before it can populate the cache. A consistently six-second Booklet response can therefore prevent rows from ever rendering despite the 20-second HTTP deadline. The focused slow-snapshot test covers the snapshot request, not this subsequent enrichment.\n\nRemedy: Keep in-flight Booklet reads alive across snapshot replacements or coordinate snapshot and enrichment work so it can finish within the existing deadline; retain cancellation on disconnect and access changes.\n\nStatic review; not claimed as a browser reproduction.",
