          "body": "[Local Codex: code-review] Handle absent Booklet states and options when sorting\n\nReviewed head: 8698a1e640ca70fcbeb43f1eddbd04ca2aa0718b\n\nThe state-column list is the union of states from all displayed Booklets, but the comparator dereferences each row's state definition and selected option whenever that row has any bookletStates object. A row with a different Booklet, an unset state, or an outdated option makes this throw. The error propagates through the subscription into the sessions BehaviorSubject, terminating monitor updates instead of sorting the rows.\n\nRemedy: Resolve each state and option defensively, including the defined default where appropriate, and use a stable fallback for missing or obsolete values. Add coverage for mixed Booklets and partially populated state objects.\n\nStatic review; not claimed as a browser reproduction.",
